{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world","id":195709,"title":"\"WoD 20\" portrayal of the real world","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-12T13:22:54-07:00","id":195709,"title":"\"WoD 20\" portrayal of the real world","content":"<i><u>Preface</u></i>.<br /> <br /> Ah, Anniversary Editions of cWoD gamelines! To say that after their announcement a few years ago \u201c<a href=\"https://github-camo.global.ssl.fastly.net/f0f2137c670353f4573810d8d7d6c6b8848ee5ad/687474703a2f2f692e696d6775722e636f6d2f4b5761316b2e6a7067\" target=\"_blank\">there was much rejoicing</a>\u201d would be an enormous understatement. All die-hard fans who, so to speak, have kept the light of the original \u201cWorld of Darkness\u201d bright through all these years really expected a lot from the various \u201c20s\u201d. Not just another chance to revisit well-known settings \u2013 there were enough books for that already. No, I will be so bold to suggest, that all those people wanted \u201cTheir Game\u201d in pure, platonic ideal sense of the word \u2013 without all numerous flaws and inconsistencies of the previous editions, up to date for our modern rapidly changing time and, yet, the same in spirit and essence.<br /> <br /> I first learned about WoD long time ago \u2013 in 2001, via my elder brothers borrowing from friends an obvious Diablo-clone known as \u201cVtM: The Redemption\u201d. While I won\u2019t consider such CRPG sub-genre as \u201cHack\u2019n\u2019Slash RPG\u201d as some sort of deep, thought provoking art piece, I\u2019m also find it enjoyable sometime. But this very game tore all stereotypes and thought-patterns that I\u2019ve always associated with such games. There was a feeling of belonging to some even bigger game universe, gleaned through often convoluted way the game tried to present its own plot and background. But most shocking of all (at least for the younger me) was the unavoidable fact of your hero\u2019s transformation into the vampire (and how!). I still remember, how I asked my brother not to sell \u201chuman\u201d health potions that he encountered during his further playthrough. Why? Because I was dead sure that, maybe in the middle of the game, or a little bit further, our brave Kristof would be transformed back into mortal. Oh, my naivety!<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve played the game for some time and then my brothers returned it. I\u2019ve forgot about all this vampire business until 2004. Prior to the launching of \u201cVtM: The Bloodlines\u201d one of the magazines I\u2019ve bought regularly published an article about the WoD universe. The \u201cBig Three\u201d game lines were discussed at length, others got lesser attention and there were also some very nice illustrations. But for me most awesome of all was that on CD that came with the magazine there were a \u201cVTM Quickstart\u201d pdf, some charsheet scans (of all Dark Ages gamelines!) and MET version of WtA (2<sup>nd</sup> ed). It was 2004, I was 17 \u2013 a very romantic age, they say. What I\u2019ve read blew out my mind. I\u2019ve never played DnD (but knew what it was), and started playing table top RPGs only in 2002. WoD became my second game system that I\u2019ve ever played.<br /> <br /> Of all the infatuations that I\u2019ve acquired in 2004 now only 3 remains \u2013 Cthulhu Mythos, WarHammer 40k and WoD.<br /> <br /> My first \u201cpaper\u201d WoD book that I\u2019ve ever read was \u201cThe Ends of Empire\u201d for WtO. I own WtO cores of both eds. Personally, I\u2019ve always loved the 1<sup>st</sup> ed core more because of it\u2019s illustrations, awesome setting history piece and feelings of sweet melancholia and nostalgia. The fact that my copy of WtO 1<sup>st</sup> ed bears the marks of its previous owner(s), like stains from some unidentified snacks didn\u2019t devalue it in my eyes.<br /> <br /> The latest addition to my collection of printed WoD books occurred a year and a half ago under very unusual circumstances. Knowing that I like WoD (after all, he was my player for a long time!) one of my friends managed to buy me a special present for the upcoming End of The World of 2012. He and his wife, plus another of my friends came all their way to the military base where I at that time was serving my stint in Army. They presented me with garishly wrapped bundle and asked me not to open till The End of the World. I\u2019ve managed to restrain myself for 3 long days. After that I unceremoniously exhumed my presents from their paper grave. What I\u2019ve found was just incredible \u2013 Mage 1<sup>st</sup> ed Core and Mage Storyteller\u2019s Handbook! As I\u2019m printing these they are lying safely on my bookshelf unaware of where they have spent several months and what kind of journey it was for them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m writing all these bits of personal history just to explain one thing \u2013 I really, really love WoD despite its numerous flaws. And I really, really, really hoped that this new \u201cAnniversary Ed\u201d thing would transform \u201cThe WoD that Was\u201d into \u201cMy Game\u201d. I\u2019ve hoped that a lot of system flaws, cranky rules, plot holes, batshit crazines of some authors that was allowed to assume printed form would be made \u201cpoof!\u201d. But most important for me, was the desperate hope that this time all those fine people that are working on WoD-20 products would avoid hamfisted, unbelievable and often quite offensive portrayal of real world countries, their histories and people that live there.<br /> <br /> You see, I\u2019m Russian, from Russia who lives in Russia. To say that the portrayal of all things Russian in cWoD was horrible, lame, prejudiced, biased and full of stereotypes would be like saying that \u201ca lot of people died in WW2\u201d. But, you know what? I actually found some excuses for all those authors who had the misfortune to mention Russia and its neighbors in their books. \u201cIt's not their fault, really. Well, they didn\u2019t have Google or Wikipedia in 90s, or anyone Russian speaking on hand while they had to write about things they don\u2019t know. And, besides, other countries/ethnicities often suffered the same poor treatment. Or just author\u2019s laziness.\u201d<br /> <br /> Naturally, I was really hopeful that now during our Global Age with its near limitless opportunities and all-pervasive Internet new cWoD books would give my country a justice and portray it realistically, not like some backward Ruritania. Also, I really, really hoped that this time around, in this form of art that is writing RPGs, our good developers and authors would avoid some widespread stereotypes and misconceptions that are often presented as \u201cwell known facts\u201d and \u201ccommon knowledge\u201d about Russia, that previous books of cWoD were literally choke-full.<br /> <br /> The main attributes of Russian stereotyping in all forms of fiction are:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Vodka. In Russia everyone drink it like water, from newborns to the elderly.</li> <li>Bears. Thousands of them! In Soviet Russia (tm) bears wander freely on the city streets in ushanka\u2019s, drink vodka, ride unicycles and kick the crap out of everyone with their trusty balalaykas.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balalaika\" target=\"_blank\">Balalaiaka </a>\u2013 every Russian owns one and can play it. It\u2019s like \u201cNatural skill\u201d for all Russians.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matryoshka_doll\" target=\"_blank\">Matryoshka</a> \u2013 the only toy Russian children play.</li> <li>AK-47. The weapon of \u201cTeam Evil\u201d (tm), dastardly stolen by the Soviet evil genius from the bright and talented German engineers.</li> <li>Kirillic alphabet \u2013 is just the Latin one, only more primitive. All complaints about grammatical inaccuracies are promptly ignored.</li> <li>KGB. A sinister Order of Evil that have spread its tentacles all through the Free world. Its agents are fanatically devote to the Motherland and Party, are spiteful, crafty and nearly indestructible. Nearly all Russians are connected with KGB in one form r another.</li> <li>Winter. Russia is always cowered in snow, no matter what time of the year or place. Russians can bring snow and chill with them even abroad \u2013 a well known fact widely believed by the Western Enlightened Public at least since the Great War.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ushanka\" target=\"_blank\">Ushanka</a> (and other \u201ctypical Russian clothes\u201d). Russian are either too poor (or too stupid) to wear anything else. With the communist simbology.</li> <li>Churches with onion domes and wooden huts (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izba\" target=\"_blank\">izbas</a>). The must have in any portrayal of Russia. Without them audience may not even believe that it\u2019s Russia (even with bears in ushankas drinking vodka in winter).</li> <li>Ivan the Terrible and Oprichnina \u2013 another proof of the \u201cunique bloodthirstiness and brutality\u201d of all Russians.</li> <li>Cossacks \u2013 Elite of the Russian Army (even in the Soviet period), the bearded <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papaha\" target=\"_blank\"><i>papakha</i></a> wearing bloody bastards good only for staging <i>pogroms</i>.</li> <li>The Red Army \u2013 consist slightly less then entirely of wearing winter-uniform (despite climate and time of the year) poor sods of all ages (as if people here serves in Army their entire life) riding either Bear Cavalry, \u201cMammoth\u201d tank or \u201cKirov\u201d war zeppelin. Russians ultimately don\u2019t know how to fight and are using exclusively \u201czerg-rush\u201d tactics.</li> <li>Red color, \u201cHammer and Sickle\u201d \u2013 must be everywhere. Even in portrayal of modern Russia \u2013 otherwise, how would enlightened Westerner realize it is Russia?</li> <li>Everyday life \u2013 all Russian men are hulkish brutes that work either for KGB or for Mafiyah or for some combination of the two. Russian women are either a seductive femme-fatales with the top-model looks, or just ugly as Hell. Naturally, all work for KGB, but constantly dream of defection.</li> <li>Beard. All Russian men must be bearded. Period. Nothing, even facts and logic, can go in the way of it.</li> <li>\u201cComrade\u201d and \u201cNazdaroffye\u201d \u2013 Russians really say that all the time \u2013 if Hollywood is sure of it, then why doubt?</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <br /> These and some other no less silly stereotypes were often found in cWoD books, but, as I\u2019ve already said \u2013 I won\u2019t judge them.<br /> <br /> What I want to talk about here is how the \u201cAnniversary WoD\u201d, i.e. the cWoD produced by the Onyx Path team deals with national stereotyping issue and all inconsistencies in the portrayal of real world and history (Dark Ages are coming\u2026) on the example of Russia. For me \u2013 it\u2019s a big deal, because the book may be even well-written, or contain some really strong or tear-jerking message \u2013 but it\u2019s all momentarily lost for me, when I read something extremely stereotyping (or just plain untrue). As I\u2019m sure on this message board there are users and WoD fans from all around the globe, I would like to hear their own \u201cWTF I\u2019m reading about my city/country/subculture/people?!\u201d moments, they\u2019ve got after reading new \u201c20s\u201d books.<br /> <br /> In my next post I would discuss what I\u2019ve found in new \u201cV20\u201d books concerning Russia and environs and what I think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T17:15:10-07:00","id":195833,"title":"","content":"So... you're upset about how Russians are portrayed in a fictional world where taking stereotypes and cranking them up past 11 is the norm?<br /> Hell, have you SEEN what they do to anything else? Native Americans? Gamers? Coorporations? Americans? Pagans, Christians, etc., etc.. Everyone is fair game, even the writers themselves are portrayed as crazy over-the-top characters who murder babies and stay so stoned that they don't know that they're being influenced by demons as they write fictional game settings that corrupt their own players... <br /> <br /> So, yes... have they stereotyped Russians? Sure! Have they drawn from what Americans might recognize and amped it up so that folks outside of Russia might recognize it? (A formori bear standing in front of Chernobyl, for instance)? Sure! Is it unlike anything else they've done that to? Not at all. It's part of the WoD... a setting of extreme characterizations, caricatures, and hyperbole.<br /> <br /> At least they didn't write about a bare-chested horse-riding, war-on-the-West, homophobic papakha-wearingPresident of Russia who came out of the KGB and wants to turn the country back to Soviet Russia and reclaim its old territories through military cohesion and firepower... That would just be a ridiculous CWoD-style villain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T18:27:36-07:00","id":195897,"title":"","content":"oWoD was racist as hell in a lot of regards; just look at the treatment of Romani (somebody said &quot;Yes, let's make a book with a slur for a title, and base it around Blood Purity,&quot; and nobody thought to stop them) or pretty much everyone in Asia. The various X20 games seem to be doing their best to cut back on a lot of shit, but I hold fast to my old mantra - <i>high hopes, low expectations</i> - and write angry forum posts when I do.<br /> <br /> So rage on, brother (or sister, or gender-neutral word of companionship ending in -er).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-12T20:35:40-07:00","id":195966,"title":"","content":"Sometimes cWoD really did read like <a href=\"http://www.amazon.com/The-Clumsiest-People-Europe-Bad-Tempered/dp/1596911506\" target=\"_blank\">The Clumsiest People in Europe</a>. <br /> <br /> Awkward confession time; I jumped into this thread from reading the title to air my own, very, <i>very</i> minor annoyance.<br /> Then I read of all the embarrassing stereotypes (not that I really forgot) and it wasn't worth it. <br /> <br /> One last thing; after the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2013_extreme_weather_events\" target=\"_blank\">last winter</a>, which seemed to last forever, I'm rather warming up to the Ushanka hat myself,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T12:06:56-07:00","id":196512,"title":"","content":"<b>VtM-20 </b><br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><u>Dust to Dust.</u></li> </ol><br /> <br /> After his uncompromising, brutal and violent \u201cTribebook Red Talons\u201d and \u201cBreedbook Rokea\u201d Matt \u201cBlack Hat\u201d McFarland became &quot;Chuck Norris of WtA gameline&quot;. The only things I\u2019ve ever heard from the people who read his Wer-books were \u201cHell yeah! That\u2019s the way to portray Wers! Matt is a great author!\u201d. And, honestly, I cannot disagree with them \u2013 Mr. McFarland is really very good <i>WtA</i> author. Also, his advises and short essays on how to run/play games that appeared in various books and on his personal blog (like \u201cWhat makes a beautiful player?\u201d) are often well-written and useful. And the parts that he\u2019d written in \u201cSpirit Slayers\u201d for the HtV are another proof that he still can deliver an excellent game materiel.<br /> <br /> Well, at least when he is writing for gamelines that:<br /> <br /> a) Suit his quite specific style<br /> b) He is actually interested in and knows a lot of stuff about.<br /> <br /> The first cracks in the nearly perfect visage of Matt \u201cChuck Norris\u201d McFarland that I had for a long time appeared after reading Dark Ages Werewolf. Well, I understand perfectly, why one of the main WtA authors was asked to not only became one of the authors of this historical corebook for the Werewolf line, but also as the developer of all Dark Ages game line, i.e. kinda guy in charge of all crunch/fluff things. Matt has his own distinct writing style so you can unmistakably notice where the parts that he actually wrote are. And one of the lines in the Circle of the Red description (written, supposedly, by him) about the attacks on the greatest Warder of the Men city septs/caerns goes:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<i>As the years passed, caerns in London, Kiev, Moscow, Beograd (sic!), Cologne and Paris came under attack and were claimed by this new foe</i>\u201d </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? And I\u2019m talking not about the typo here. I\u2019m talking about mentioning Moscow in the same line as the other large medieval European cities. I understand that Moscow is probably one of the few Russian cities that the average American has ever heard off, but I was under the impression that game developers and authors of the game set in the historical time period <i>maybe</i> should do some research beforehand? Yes, I know \u2013 that\u2019s sounds crazy! Mentioning a developing but still pretty much frontier town that had been founded some years prior to 1147, that had often changed owners and that had a total population of about <i>5000</i> max (if you count nearby estates and villages) along with some long established and more populous cities (Kiev as the most populous Russian city had 40k citizens prior to the Mongol invasion) <i>makes no sense</i>. Why mention Moscow, but not, say, Berlin? It was founded approximately in the same time as Moscow and had, probably, the same demographics and status as well. Mentioning Berlin will also make no sense at all and, AFAIK it\u2019s never mentioned in any of the Dark Ages books.<br /> <br /> If you think that mentioning of Moscow in this instance was some sort of odd mistake, an easily forgotten case of a bad research that has nothing to do with the rest of the book, then how can you explain this passage from the Lithuania\u2019s description?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<i>Lithuania</i><i> sits to the south of Latvia, between the empire of Tartars and Muscovy and Christendom</i>\u201d. </div> </div> </div>Erm, should I unnecessarily remind everyone that the game of DA:W is set in 1230? Long before the Mongolian invasion? And Moscow at that time was just another small town of Vladimir-Suzdal princedom? The way the author here (I\u2019m not sure if it was Matt, but he, as the chief developer, is nonetheless responsible) describes Lithuania is correct\u2026 for the 14 centaury. Also, what\u2019s the matter of singling out \u201cMuscovy\u201d as not being part of the \u201cChristendom\u201d? Russians, what, have experienced some kind of unexpected and un-documented pagan revival while no-one was looking?<br /> <br /> And that was only the beginning of downfall of Mr. McFarland from his pedestal of the \u201cUnsullied WoD Writer\u201d. Then someone decided that it would be such a swell idea to invite him to write something for the \u201cInfinite Tapestry\u201d book for the Mage\u2026 which he did with all the subtlety of a wrecking ball while treating the old material. Finally, he finished off the CtD line in the \u201cTime of Judgement\u201d book with his signature style, i.e. pretty much ignoring nearly everything that was written before hand (i.e. don\u2019t givin\u2019 a damn to all this \u201cGame of Thrones meets War for Independence\u201d\u2026 thing) and just gave us a story about Palpatin-Milege, 2 \u201cwhimpers\u201d and 2 \u201cbangs!\u201d that are, despite all his attempts to deny it, were really just a \u201cFeyHammer 30k\u201d.<br /> <br /> And this worthy individual was asked to write an adventure for the \u201creborn\u201d VtM20. After all, he\u2019d written\u2026 some stuff\u2026as one of the co-authors\u2026 for VtM in the past! Long, long time ago, nothing memorable, but he did!<br /> <br /> And \u201cDust to Dust\u201d probably (just probably!) might have become a good well-written adventure if the good people of the \u201cOnyx Path\u201d hired someone with the nerves of steel, who\u2019s job would be to use a cattle prod on Mr. McFarland every time he goes bat-shit off topic in fluff or starts to imagine that players need the WtA level stats for antagonists.<br /> <br /> And of course, enough electrically charged motivation would have done something to this character:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<b>Lazlo Varga</b><br /> <i>Lazlo Varga died years ago in Detroit, but that didn\u2019t stop him. A mortal necromancer of some skill before his death, the bullet in his heart did nothing but force his hand. He activated a ring he had stolen in Kiev some years back \u2014 a ring that supposedly belonged to Rasputin himself. According to reports, the ring allowed its wearer to survive any wound</i>.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Oh, how original! A typical Eastern European Evil Character (tm) named <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/L%C3%A1szl%C3%B3_Varga_(footballer)\" target=\"_blank\">after some real-life person</a>! And look \u2013 this book is so faithful in its early VtM editions references that it even makes Rasputin homage! It\u2019s another \u201cwell-known fact\u201d for the Enlightened Western Audience that Rasputin was \u201cnight indestructible Russian Mad-Monk/Evil Sorcerer with dreadful powers and enormous libido\u201d. That he was so hard to kill had nothing to do with<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The low-grade Cyanide dissolving in pastries that Rasputin ate in Yusupov\u2019s house.</li> <li>The first \u201cmortal shot\u201d was dealt by prince Yusupov (a well know transvestite) with his lady\u2019s Derringer.</li> <li>The final shots were delivered by the leader of rabid anti-Semitic and chauvinistic party <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Purishkevich\" target=\"_blank\">Purishkevich</a> who had very bad eyesight.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> No! It was magic! Speaking of which how did the (supposedly!) Rasputin\u2019s ring turned out in Kiev? Or, what, it was just another way to show the vast geographical knowledge of Russia by the author which he already demonstrated in his Dark Ages books? Hey, more importantly \u2013 would the plot of the adventure itself suffered if all this \u201cRasputin connection\u201d or mention of Kiev were left out? Nope, not at all. So\u2026 what was the point? To convince readers even more of this character sinister Eastern Europeaness by making references to obvious stereotypes? What was the point?<br /> <br /> And how should I understand this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<i>If the characters wish to study his necromancy, they find that it has its roots in Eastern European magical practices. Though it\u2019s different in theory and basis from most forms of Necromancy that vampires practice, it all works the same from a game perspective</i>.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Uhmm, Mr. McFarland, I don\u2019t know if you will ever read my post, but, nevertheless, I\u2019d like to ask you about all these \u201cEastern European magical practices\u201d. You see, as an Eastern Europe (as if it\u2019s some sort of homogeneous territory!) resident I can\u2019t recall any necromantic practices in the region countries\u2019 folklore. Yeah, shocking, I know, but myths and fairy tales here dodn\u2019t mention rituals for raising undead legions of marauding zombies or making restless souls of the departed to make your bidding.<br /> <br /> How did our power-hungry, brutal and merciless Eastern European necromancer (honestly, I can\u2019t say this aloud without laughing) looks like \u2013 or more importantly \u2013 on which real life person is he based? Hungary, after all, is a country where all kind of people live, so his appearance may be just anything the author decides to give him! Did he look like the great Hungarian poet, patriot and revolutionary <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S%C3%A1ndor_Pet%C5%91fi\" target=\"_blank\">S\u00e1ndor Pet\u0151fi</a>? Or Karoly Takacs (they have this nice <a href=\"http://badassoftheweek.com/index.cgi?ccpage=1&amp;ccid=674113616992\" target=\"_blank\">Badass of the Week strip about him</a>)?<br /> <br /> Naah \u2013 are you kidding? Did you, after reading so far, expect anything but even more clich\u00e9s?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201c<i>Lazlo is a muscular, solidly built man in his late 40s. He shaves his head and wears a full beard\u2026 He dresses in simple clothing and expensive, sturdy boots. He speaks with a thick Hungarian accent</i>.\u201d </div> </div> </div><br /> So, basically he is just another lame \u201c<a href=\"http://images.rottentomatoes.com/images/movie/gallery/1131153/photo_14_hires.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Rasputin</a>\u201d from the \u201cHellboy\u201d movie, which is also just another \u201chulkish standard-issue Eastern European Bad Guy\u201d. Was it done deliberately by the author, to save all future Storytellers that would run \u201cDust to Dust\u201d some time, by allowing them to say: \u201cOk, players \u2013 you see Rasputin from the \u201cHellboy\u201d\u201d \u201cOoooh! He must be a bad guy!\u201d<br /> <br /> What was all this point of creating some stereotypical \u201cEastern European\u201d character for the VtM adventure? In what way does the fact that he is a Hungarian influence the story? In no way whatsoever \u2013 he could be just as easily made Portuguese, Albanian or Armenian. Lazlo Varga is a walking stereotype, a two-dimensional NPC that is just a collection Eastern European tropes, bringing home to players and storytellers alike ages old idea, that \u201cEastern Europe is Mordor of the Earth! Everything is baaaaaaad here!\u201d. This kind of portrayal is either a demonstration of laziness and/or of unshakable beliefs of the author in all stereotypes he is referencing here. Strangely enough, but I don\u2019t consider all these kind of cheesiness as a mark of \u201cdoing justice\u201d and \u201creviving the spirit\u201d of VtM. All these makes already far from perfect (to put it mildly) adventure even worse.<br /> <br /> But Mr. McFarland\u2019s \u201coutstanding\u201d material just pale before another VtM20 product I gonna discuss in my next post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 07-16-2014, 10:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T14:18:49-07:00","id":196553,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">As a reminder, it is totally fine to share opinions, positive or negative, about WoD writing, but please make sure your critique is of the writing itself, not the person who wrote it.</span> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=196512#post196512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>VtM-20 </b>[*]The first \u201cmortal shot\u201d was dealt by prince Yusupov (a well know transvestite) with his lady\u2019s Derringer.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:red\">While derringers have a small caliber and are therefore less lethal than larger guns, the fact that they were popular sidearms for women, and the gender identity and presentation of the person firing one, have nothing whatsoever to do with the lethality. Comments that denigrate groups of people are not acceptable.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T15:09:28-07:00","id":196585,"title":"","content":"I get your point though im from the opinion that for gritty realism NWoD is the game to go while OWoD is the game to play trenchcoat katanas in a world full of 90s stereotypes.<br /> <br /> Like NWoD is totally trying to be the more mature game and judges you if you dont have fun its way. While OWoD is the game that tells you &quot;Its okay to sometimes want to play a Romani with magical power base on purity of blood&quot; or a &quot;Drunken Irish werewolf. Its cool, i wont judge you&quot;.<br /> <br /> Thats my view and is not just Russia. South America is misrepresented as well, at least Russia you could say is seen as the same sort of misguided &quot;coolness&quot; similar to Japan in the 90s. South America? We have mention in werewolf on the rainforest that's about it. No matter that almost nobody outside of brazil care about the Rainforest in the rest of South America.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world#post195709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i><u>Preface</u></i>.<br /> The main attributes of Russian stereotyping in all forms of fiction are:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Vodka. In Russia everyone drink it like water, from newborns to the elderly.</li> <li>Bears. Thousands of them! In Soviet Russia (tm) bears wander freely on the city streets in ushanka\u2019s, drink vodka, ride unicycles and kick the crap out of everyone with their trusty balalaykas.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Balalaika\" target=\"_blank\">Balalaiaka </a>\u2013 every Russian owns one and can play it. It\u2019s like \u201cNatural skill\u201d for all Russians.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Matryoshka_doll\" target=\"_blank\">Matryoshka</a> \u2013 the only toy Russian children play.</li> <li>AK-47. The weapon of \u201cTeam Evil\u201d (tm), dastardly stolen by the Soviet evil genius from the bright and talented German engineers.</li> <li>Kirillic alphabet \u2013 is just the Latin one, only more primitive. All complaints about grammatical inaccuracies are promptly ignored.</li> <li>KGB. A sinister Order of Evil that have spread its tentacles all through the Free world. Its agents are fanatically devote to the Motherland and Party, are spiteful, crafty and nearly indestructible. Nearly all Russians are connected with KGB in one form r another.</li> <li>Winter. Russia is always cowered in snow, no matter what time of the year or place. Russians can bring snow and chill with them even abroad \u2013 a well known fact widely believed by the Western Enlightened Public at least since the Great War.</li> <li><a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ushanka\" target=\"_blank\">Ushanka</a> (and other \u201ctypical Russian clothes\u201d). Russian are either too poor (or too stupid) to wear anything else. With the communist simbology.</li> <li>Churches with onion domes and wooden huts (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Izba\" target=\"_blank\">izbas</a>). The must have in any portrayal of Russia. Without them audience may not even believe that it\u2019s Russia (even with bears in ushankas drinking vodka in winter).</li> <li>Ivan the Terrible and Oprichnina \u2013 another proof of the \u201cunique bloodthirstiness and brutality\u201d of all Russians.</li> <li>Cossacks \u2013 Elite of the Russian Army (even in the Soviet period), the bearded <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papaha\" target=\"_blank\"><i>papakha</i></a> wearing bloody bastards good only for staging <i>pogroms</i>.</li> <li>The Red Army \u2013 consist slightly less then entirely of wearing winter-uniform (despite climate and time of the year) poor sods of all ages (as if people here serves in Army their entire life) riding either Bear Cavalry, \u201cMammoth\u201d tank or \u201cKirov\u201d war zeppelin. Russians ultimately don\u2019t know how to fight and are using exclusively \u201czerg-rush\u201d tactics.</li> <li>Red color, \u201cHammer and Sickle\u201d \u2013 must be everywhere. Even in portrayal of modern Russia \u2013 otherwise, how would enlightened Westerner realize it is Russia?</li> <li>Everyday life \u2013 all Russian men are hulkish brutes that work either for KGB or for Mafiyah or for some combination of the two. Russian women are either a seductive femme-fatales with the top-model looks, or just ugly as Hell. Naturally, all work for KGB, but constantly dream of defection.</li> <li>Beard. All Russian men must be bearded. Period. Nothing, even facts and logic, can go in the way of it.</li> <li>\u201cComrade\u201d and \u201cNazdaroffye\u201d \u2013 Russians really say that all the time \u2013 if Hollywood is sure of it, then why doubt?</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>It is bad i like your super wrong version of Russia? Yes? though so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-13-2014, 06:12 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T16:17:41-07:00","id":196602,"title":"","content":"LokiRavenSpeak, I'm gonna stop you there; no part of oWoD's treatment of the Romani was acceptable. Printing a game with a slur for a title and nothing but fetishization of moronic old stereotypes is not an acceptable release, and there is nothing &quot;cool&quot; about it. Neither is the Ravnos being consistently referred to as the same slur (would it be acceptable if the Assamites primary nickname was &quot;Ragheads?&quot; or if one of the clans had the N word as a nickname? Didn't think so.) and suffering from <i>a fucking magical compulsion to steal shit</i>; the later &quot;fix&quot; (they aren't driven to steal, they're driven to <i>a wide range of crimes!</i>) is no better.<br /> <br /> I don't care if I'm stepping on your fun, there's nothing okay about that kind of bullshit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":281,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","user":"atamajakki","date":". 07-13-2014, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T17:22:53-07:00","id":196612,"title":"","content":"So how it is any worse than fetishization WoD has have with Asia for most of it history, even now (Mage quickstarter: katana the best sword?)? Im not saying is good or bad. Im saying old wod isnt really based on the real world. Is more like a caricature of pop-culture things that were cool in 90s. And wheter was sensible or not (It wasnt really), romani culture had/has a certain &quot;coolness&quot; that Gypsies book tried to exploit and fail. <br /> <br /> I get wanting a more realistic approach to the setting but OWoD is like the movie &quot;Black Dynamite&quot; is fun by its own misguided ignorance and exaggerations. Hell, you could probably play the &quot;fetishization of moronic old steretypes&quot; in a lots OWoD. Imbreed Russian royalty (SFs), Drunken irish (Fianna), angry femnazis (BFs), ASIA IS PLAIN BETTER THAN EVERYTHING (in lots of books)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T17:36:52-07:00","id":196614,"title":"","content":"It's plenty worse. Romani have a long-held bias against them as chronic thieves, swindlers, and any number of unseemly reputations; oWoD's answer to this was to say &quot;The vampires that are traditionally Romani? Yeah, they have a <i>supernatural</i> <i>compulsion</i> to live up to the bullshit stereotype that leads to persecution still today.&quot; It's really not on the same level as &quot;katanas are so cool,&quot; though I have plenty of beef with oWoD's treatment of Asia. <br /> <br /> Black Dynamite was a self-aware satire of 1970s &quot;blaxploitation&quot; films. oWoD is never self-aware in its racist depictions of various peoples, and freely runs with stereotypes that are then defended by fans when someone says &quot;wow, that's fucked up!&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't really understand what you're aiming for here. You're freely acknowledging exploitation and admitting to ignorance and lack of sensibility, then claiming that you're not &quot;saying it's good or bad.&quot; What part of any of that is good?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T18:21:49-07:00","id":196625,"title":"","content":"First Katanas are cool is only the tip of the iceberg but still.<br /> <br /> What i mean by is neither good or bad is this. First i have to make a little comparison to NWoD going a little off theme here.<br /> <br /> NWoD has one flavor and one flavor only. Gritty realism. There is nothing silly on it and by many has being labeled flavorless because its like the real world.<br /> <br /> OWoD 90s has all the exploitation and lack of sensibility and everything but it has a very strong flavor while remaining somewhat malleable. I want to make a game with realism like NWoD? sure i can do that. I just have to remove things of the setting and its done. I want to make a game of unapologetic 90s stereotypes? Yes i can do that playing the game as it is. Want to do the same thing with NWoD? Then im gonna be having to fight the system/setting a lot (creating bloodlines, disciplines, lodge, whatever). The level of racial insensibility in a WoD games is regulated by the players/DM as they can ignore the text as written and to be honest i even doubt that OWoD isnt self aware, Tzimices with penis in the elbows and the vagina-face guy in the book comes to my mind as an example the realism and real world seriousness was left on the door.<br /> <br /> What i say is neither good nor bad? Experience. I had a player who was of romani family who enjoy the hell of playing a thieving Ravnos and im from Japanese descendant and played a haken werewolf who speaked it in fortune cookie speech. There are people who play Russian mobsters with the thickness of accents and start most phrases with &quot;In soviet Russia....&quot; Or drunken furry irish. Can i condemn them for having fun that way? Maybe i defend it because i came to the OWoD expecting a fun ride of over the top stereotypes and silliness and i just got that.<br /> <br /> I never felt that the ignorance and lack of sensibility of OWoD was mean spirited. Is a game that tells you &quot;If you want to play a stereotype i wont judge you, if you dont there is plenty of room for you too&quot; and it has a certain charm to it. But if you are those people who are bothered by the mere presence of stereotypes then NWoD is there. Gritty realism getting a new edition right now.<br /> <br /> What part of it is good? Honestly sometimes is fun to play this over the top stereotypes, sometimes is fun to see the setting and have a laugh at how plain silly and wrong it is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 07-13-2014, 09:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T12:25:13-07:00","id":197088,"title":"","content":"There is a difference between satire of racism and satire that is racist. Much of OWoD was the latter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T13:02:22-07:00","id":197114,"title":"","content":"Anyone with a degree in history or/and cultural studies could go on for days redlining things that are just wrong in oWoD. But let's not forget that the American authors have written most of this stuff based on very limited knowledge. Slavic belief/spirituality for example is based on a single russian book, which deals only with eastern Slavic belief (how do I know? Nomenclature, the term &quot;Koldun&quot; was a dead giveaway). The western and southern Slavic beliefs are completely left out. The pre-christian Slavic shamanic/priestly activity was labeled as Germanic in a Mage supplement. This doesn't excuse bad research and stereotypes though, as many of the mistakes were just sloppy. I dealt with it by rewriting things that were problematic, removing stuff that shouldn't be there and adding things that should, like the Fianna in France (Gauls!).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To a player who wanted his character to attend a very &quot;special&quot; school:<br /> There is no Charles F. Lupus school for gifted werewolves.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/971-arag","name":"Arag","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar971_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T15:06:54-07:00","id":198255,"title":"","content":"Now, some answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=195833#post195833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>So... you're upset about how Russians are portrayed in a fictional world where taking stereotypes and cranking them up past 11 is the norm?<br /> Hell, have you SEEN what they do to anything else? Native Americans? Gamers? Coorporations? Americans? Pagans, Christians, etc., etc.. Everyone is fair game, even the writers themselves are portrayed as crazy over-the-top characters who murder babies and stay so stoned that they don't know that they're being influenced by demons as they write fictional game settings that corrupt their own players...<br /> <br /> So, yes... have they stereotyped Russians? Sure! Have they drawn from what Americans might recognize and amped it up so that folks outside of Russia might recognize it? (A formori bear standing in front of Chernobyl, for instance)? Sure! Is it unlike anything else they've done that to? Not at all. It's part of the WoD... a setting of extreme characterizations, caricatures, and hyperbole</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d like to ask everyone \u2013 where did exactly, in what book, booklet or article, did the WhiteWolfers say in unquestionable terms, that their game world is \u201ca collection of stereotypes turned up to 11\u201d? The fact that the game-as-written often appeared like that is without doubt, but was it the official stance?<br /> <br /> Correct me if I\u2019m wrong, but \u201cWhite Wolfs\u201d from the very beginning attempted to address the gender, racial, religious and sexuality problems and conflicts, giving (or, at least, attempting to give) a fair portrayal of often persecuted or discriminated groups (and only later all this degraded to the typical \u201cTokenism\u201d). Early WtA books are full of authors\u2019 commentaries on the spirituality, ecology and similar topics. Again, correct me if I\u2019m wrong, but they were probably the first game company to include LGTB NPCs (and providing one in the WtO 1<sup>st</sup> ed as an example character in the Character Creation chapter). I can\u2019t really remember any book, where they would portray one of several characters belonging to one particular racial group with the extremely stereotypical description of their:<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li><a href=\"http://i1.ytimg.com/vi/hriKiBbw3nU/maxresdefault.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Dietary preferences</a>.</li> <li>Universal predisposition <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=fhRHCGYiWX4\" target=\"_blank\">to play certain musical instruments and possession of said instruments by default</a>.</li> <li>Natural involvement with <a href=\"http://images.tvrage.com/screencaps/27/5266/159657.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">all sorts of the criminal activity</a>.</li> <li>Caricatural <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iUZvO36zm6Y\" target=\"_blank\">gender roles</a> and \u201ctypical\u201d <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=RYvplvdHmlw\" target=\"_blank\">gender behavior</a>.</li> <li>Distinct<a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XgpRjZKM_Tw\" target=\"_blank\"> way of communication</a> with each other and with the \u201cnormal\u201d people.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> If \u201cWhite Wolfs\u201d decided that doing that would be outright offensive, discriminatory or even racist, then why didn\u2019t they gave the same treatment to all other social and ethnic categories? More importantly \u2013 will the \u201cOnix Path\u201d authors use the same double-standards in their work on the \u201cWoD20\u201d or can we now, in the 21 centaury, expect some improvements?<br /> <br /> As for your, Torakhan, comments, that it\u2019s okay to portray everything over the top. May I presume, that American gamers who read that kind of grotesque in-game portrayal of something that they knew quite well (say, Chicago), they could potentially divide the fact from the deliberately biased fiction. That\u2019s when the subject is familiar for them. But if it\u2019s a description of something they know not so well, or know nothing at all, they tend to believe every stereotype in that presentation, not doubting for a minute, that they are reading something else but truth. Despite all the disclaimers that \u201cYou can\u2019t study history/geography through WoD books\u201d, people, who don\u2019t study history and geography through normal means (i.e. the majority) would anyway gain their \u201cvast knowledge\u201d from even such sources.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=195833#post195833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At least they didn't write about a bare-chested horse-riding, war-on-the-West, homophobic papakha-wearingPresident of Russia who came out of the KGB and wants to turn the country back to Soviet Russia and reclaim its old territories through military cohesion and firepower... That would just be a ridiculous CWoD-style villain.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What a nice collections of clich\u00e9s as presented by the \u201cFree Objective Western Media\u201d we have here! Well, \u201cpapakha-wearing\u201d part is, obviously, your own addition, after reading my first post. Tell me, Torakhan, did you believe it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-15T20:18:35-07:00","id":198515,"title":"","content":"OP: As a writer, editor, and developer for Onyx Path, I must say, we do try. We make every effort to improve regularly. You might notice some of that in the V20 Dark Ages development posts; it's been a big part of our priorities list to deal with cultural topics in a better light. We don't always succeed. But we do make the effort. We appreciate the discussion, and try to take it all to heart.<br /> <br /> Thank you.<br /> <br /> That said?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world#post195709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Bears. Thousands of them! In Soviet Russia (tm) bears wander freely on the city streets in ushanka\u2019s, drink vodka, ride unicycles and kick the crap out of everyone with their trusty balalaykas.</li> </ol></div> </div> </div> </div>I draw the line at bears. Bears are awesome and scary and I will never apologize for adding more bears. What I will offer though is to offer more diverse representations of bears. We won't just feature Russian bears, but we'll focus on polar bears, grizzly bears, black bears, and even koala and panda bears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>David A Hill Jr </b><br /> Freelance Writer<br /> Independent Game Designer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/70-machineiv","name":"MachineIV","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar70_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1791"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T02:40:07-07:00","id":198752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> At least they didn't write about a bare-chested horse-riding, war-on-the-West, homophobic papakha-wearingPresident of Russia who came out of the KGB and wants to turn the country back to Soviet Russia and reclaim its old territories through military cohesion and firepower... That would just be a ridiculous CWoD-style villain. </div> </div> </div>I do plan making President Putin as a Mage, though I'm giving him more President Valentine treatment. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The point is, lots of charm of OWoD is its campiness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T08:56:58-07:00","id":198998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world#post195709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankly, I don't get the problem with stereotypes. WoD &quot;regional&quot; books aren't tourist guides or national geographic issues, they are book games concerned with giving players who probably aren't from the region a vague idea of the area, some local flavour and hints for playing a lot.<br /> So they don't need to be really, or even averagely, rigorous. A book about Russia need to give players some good ideas and exotic settings, so vodka, bears, winter and beard are a good starting point (and if you ask me, I'd like to throw in even a couple troikas [the sleigh]).<br /> If these notion are inaccurate, from a native point of view, well... too bad, but it's a game.<br /> <br /> Let me clarify.<br /> I'm italian, but if you look at italy in the WoD you get the Giovanni (incestuous, necrophile mafiosi) with their minor branch, the Rossellini (sadist perfecionists), the Puttanesca (mafiosi bullies), the Della Passaglia (exoticist scholar dabblers) and Ghiberti (slavers). This is clearly a hill of stereotypes pressed togheter, and in other books where they speak of italy you get at best a sensation of debauched <i>ancient regime</i> and monsters hidden under each tile you step.<br /> (ok, I haven't read EVERY cWoD books, but this is the general sensation).<br /> <br /> The point is, all this don't really matter.<br /> The Giovanni (and offshoots) backroung make for an excellent and richly flavoured game ambientation and all the &quot;corrupt&quot; sensation make a really good settings for a good amount of chronicles.<br /> They may sting a little from a localist point of view but, frankly, why I need to care?<br /> It's the World of Darkness, not the real world. If someone ask me for some clarification on the real italy (already happened on this forum) for the sake of making a more accurate chronicle, I'll gladly give advice. But I don't think a fictional portrait of the place where I live need to be austerely objective.<br /> Nor yours, because I'll be more attracted to staging a game in a russia rich of bears, troikas, yurts, vodka, winter and beards than a realistic russia almost too similar to my own place.<br /> This way, it's more fun .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T11:50:04-07:00","id":199135,"title":"","content":"Your error is evident in the very thread title. The cWoD never aspired to portray the real world. It's in the name: World of Darkness. Pretty much all the corebooks point out that the world is one based ob, but different from ours. In this world, things are generally darker, grittier and yes, more stereotypical. If you can't accept that, you'll sinply have to ignore most of the. published material and make your own. The stereotypes applies pretty evenly, however. Me, I for one accept that in the cWoD, scandinavians are all six-foot plus, blonde and blue-eyed beefcakes who listen to metal and worship the Norse gods. None of this is particulalry true in the real world, but there you go.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/300-hod","name":"HOD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar300_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"466"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T13:51:01-07:00","id":199226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HOD</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=199135#post199135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your error is evident in the very thread title. The cWoD never aspired to portray the real world. It's in the name: World of Darkness. Pretty much all the corebooks point out that the world is one based ob, but different from ours. In this world, things are generally darker, grittier and yes, more stereotypical. If you can't accept that, you'll sinply have to ignore most of the. published material and make your own. The stereotypes applies pretty evenly, however. Me, I for one accept that in the cWoD, scandinavians are all six-foot plus, blonde and blue-eyed beefcakes who listen to metal and worship the Norse gods. None of this is particulalry true in the real world, but there you go.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they're good at sympathizing with strange people, so when all the world is going to gehenna, scandinavian people and vampires organize for taking turns at sucking and being sucked (no pun intended). Yay, I love the scandinavian gehenna.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>====================================<br /> &quot;Worst English-language User&quot; 2011-2015, 2017 running for the 2018<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i.imgur.com/Ed6RV6Z.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></div></div> </div> </div>","edited":{"userid":515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","user":"Ryoga84","date":". 07-16-2014, 08:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/515-ryoga84","name":"Ryoga84","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"552"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-16T22:54:17-07:00","id":199704,"title":"","content":"<b>2. Anarchs unbound.</b><br /> <br /> Now, I know, that it will sound shocking for someone, but, still, when judging any RPG product I personally consider its usefulness for <i>my</i> games. I really don\u2019t care for about kilobytes of purple prose that some sourcebook\u2019s authors have included just to show how they (or their Mary/Marty Sues) are awesome. I want a product that I can use in my chronicles. The biggest trouble of all time was to find a product that would allow me to play and stage an adequate, normal and canonically accurate games set in Russia. So far, sWoD had been extremely unhelpful. No, it was downright awful. There were 3 books of VtM line that contained what could be called a \u201cVampire\\s Russia Lore\u201d. It was \u201cClanbook Brujah 1<sup>st</sup> ed\u201d, \u201cClanbook Brujah Revised\u201d and \u201cGuide to the Anarchs\u201d. About 1-2 pages each worth of \u201ccanonical Russian Lore\u201d.<br /> <br /> Each and every one of them is despicably horrible. <b><i>Each one</i></b>.<br /> <br /> You know, just yesterday I\u2019ve conducted a small experiment of sorts. On the message board where I post often there are a lot of Russians, Bulgarians, Serbs, Bosniaks, some Poles, Greeks one Brazillian and even one Canado-Italian patriot. So, I\u2019ve posted an excerpt from the \u201cGuide to the Anarchs\u201d describing Bulgaria. The first response was \u201c<i>Oh moi Boh</i>, WTF was that?!\u201d. The second would be censored everywhere. The fifth response got into a deep historical, political and socioeconomically analysis that can be summed up in \u201cEvery single sentence is wrong. What kind of drugs the author was high on while writing that piece of bovine feces?\u201d.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why, as I\u2019ve said previously in my OP, I won\u2019t discuss the original WW books here. Otherwise, I\u2019d have to write a comment about every sentence in their \u201c<i>canonical</i>\u201d descriptions of Russia, sometimes devoting several paragraphs just to describe how <i>one</i> of their sentences is plainly wrong.<br /> <br /> What I've wanted was a book, that would give a Russia a justice in the VtM setting, a book, that would allow me to draw upon it\u2019s wealth of material to set my chronicles in \u201cRussia by Night\u201d, that would be both interesting and canonically correct. While a lot of other European countries were graced with the adequate write-ups WoD-style, describing the history of vampires here, the strongholds of the Sects, the standing of various clans and etc. setting wise, Russia didn\u2019t have the same treatment. And I really, really hoped, that this time, under the \u201cOnyx Path\u201d aegis, the situation could be improved.<br /> <br /> Enter \u201cAnarchs Unbound\u201d.<br /> <br /> Just reading the list of authors already sank my expectations. So, Justin Achilli is not only the developer of the whole line \u2013 he is one the authors here. A man, who wrote \u201cClanbook Brujah revised\u201d \u2013 and I\u2019ve already gave my opinion about its \u201cRussian section\u201d. Justin \u201c<i>Everything I write is already a canon, bitches!</i>\u201d Achilli \u2013 \u201cWhite Wolves\u201d personal version of Dan \u201c<i>I don\u2019t give a damn about the fluff \u2013 lets add more comic books level of cheesiness here!</i>\u201d Abnett. An author who is both prolific and lacking in writing talent, with, apparently, nobody to tell him about his drawbacks.<br /> <br /> But, surely, after all these years, Mr. Achilli actually devoted some time to self improvement and his writing won\u2019t cause an instant gag reflex from the readers, right? Right!?<br /> <br /> The title like \u201cThe Rise of Soviet Vampirism\u201d already don\u2019t promse anything worthy, objective and useful. Because \u201cIn Soviet Russia YOU drink vampire!\u201d, or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The Russian Revolution of 1917, like most revolutions, almost immediately turned into a bloody civil war. Casualties on both sides of the conflict between the Red Bolsheviks and every Russian who opposed them numbered in the millions, with Tsar Nicholas and his family merely the most famous victims. By the time the Union of Soviet Socialist Republics was officially named, the Romanov dynasty and the hereditary nobility that had supported it since the 17th century had been swept away. The few Russian nobles to survive fled westward, to France, Britain, and beyond, for the most part to die in obscurity. Tonight, the non-claimant heir to the Tsar\u2019s throne is over 90 and lists \u201cinsurance company executive\u201d on his resume</i>. </div> </div> </div>This is the first paragraph \u2013 and already it reaches the level of crappiness, stereotypical portrayal and historical inaccuracies of <i>Ye Goode Olde WoD</i>. Did the authors know that in the 21 centaury historical facts can be checked so easily that writing such things should be just shameful?<br /> <br /> Oh, where should I start? First of all \u2013 about <i>which</i> Russia Revolution did the authors talk here? There were 2 in 1917 \u2013one in February (that toppled the Czar), another in October (the Bolshevik one). Is it too hard to remember?<br /> <br /> Next, the second sentence implies that the Russian Civil war was \u201cEbul Red Bolsheviks against the rest of Russia\u201d, which is just plainly wrong. What about the <a href=\"http://Entente Intervention\" target=\"_blank\">Entente's Intervention</a>, that drew to Russia soldiers from France, Britain, USA, Japan and even Romania ? What about German and Austro-Hungary occupied territories? What about the Czechoslovak Legion? What about Finland? What about the extensive use of Latvians and Chinese (yes, <i>Chinese</i>) by the Bolsheviks? What about all the wars that suddenly free Caucasian republics got themselves into \u2013 including a very unsuccessful one versus Turkey? Finally, what about Poland?<br /> <br /> But, no the whole Russian Civil War is covered in just a couple of sentences. One of the most dramatic periods in countries history (not to mention \u2013 real mother lode for WoD scenarios and settings) got just a couple of sentences choke full of inaccuracies.<br /> <br /> Oh, and finally \u2013 the text presumes some kind of genocide of literally all nobles in now Soviet Russia that every one noble either emigrated or were executed. Well, there were a lot of executed nobles, as well as the one who chose the exile. But not everyone. What about the general <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleksei_Brusilov\" target=\"_blank\">Aleksey Brusilov</a>? What about the writer, the &quot;Red count&quot; <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aleksey_Nikolayevich_Tolstoy\" target=\"_blank\">Aleksey Tolstoy</a>? What about diplomat count <a href=\"http://ru.wikipedia.org/wiki/%D0%98%D0%B3%D0%BD%D0%B0%D1%82%D1%8C%D0%B5%D0%B2,_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B9_%D0%90%D0%BB%D0%B5%D0%BA%D1%81%D0%B5%D0%B5%D0%B2%D0%B8%D1%87\" target=\"_blank\">Aleksey Ignatyev</a>? What about Lenin himself? And what about the mere fact that about 70% of Russian officer corps fought on the side of Bolsheviks during the Civil War, the majority of them \u2013 noble-born?<br /> <br /> See? Just one paragraph worth of several sentences, but already a commentary larger that the original! Is this the new \u201cV20\u201d that the authors strive to \u2013 as bad as the original?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>For the Russian Kindred, the Revolution actually started in 1900. Long after the rest of Europe had embraced modernization and made at least a pretense of trying to create a functional middle class, Russian gentry still held their peasants in a state of deliberate ignorance and deprivation through official state policies. By happy coincidence, these policies also fulfilled the desire of comfort-dulled vampires for massive herds that required neither maintenance nor discretion. The Tsarist Kindred, a loose confederation of Ventrue, Toreador, and Old Clan Tzimisce, were insular, arrogant, and imperious, and they generally showed little but disdain for the other clans that weren\u2019t part of their courtly society. </i> </div> </div> </div>Well, on the one hand \u2013 there is something positive in this passage. We learn that the ruling positions in Russia by night were held by Ventrue, Toreador, and Old Clan Tzimisce (the last one was deduced by the Russian Storytellers long time ago and included as a semi-canon long, long time ago). But \u2013 what about Camarilla? How did all this arrangement work? Did the Camarilla just accepted that somewhere in its domain there are towns claimed by Tzimisce (\u201c<b><i>non-Sabbat, yeah, sure, like we gonna believe it!</i></b>\u201d), but that other Camarilla aligned vampires recognize their authority and integrate them fully into the existing power structure (<i><b>what an affront for the posh Victorian vampires, I say!</b></i>). This tidbit is interesting but leaves more questions, than answers, i.e. how Russian vampires were structured pre-Revolutions?<br /> <br /> No, this paragraph is more devoted to the portraying much of doom and glum in Russia. Here, we (surprisingly, me included) find out, that the main cause for all Russian revolutions was the absence of a middle class (preferably in its idealized American iteration, with car, house and 2.5 kids), not something other like, you know, everything Grandpa Lenin already mentioned in his works? Also, I\u2019d like to see the said \u201cembrace of modernization\u201d by the \u201crest of Europe\u201d in Spain, Portugal, Italy, Greece, Bulgaria, Serbia, Austro-Hungarian Empire, Denmark and Sweden. If authors would grace us with it, I\u2019m sure it would be a fun read.<br /> <br /> Finally, an extremely hilarious part (for me at least) about how the &quot;ebul Russian <i>pomeshiks</i>&quot;, somehow, \u201cheld their peasants in a state of deliberate ignorance and deprivation through official state policies\u201d. I guess, our esteemed authors have never heard about the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emancipation_reform_of_1861\" target=\"_blank\">Emancipation reform of 1861,</a> that have freed the Russian peasants from their serfdom. So, no, Russian gentry had no power whatsoever to \u201cheld in ignorance\u201d people over whom they had virtually no power. And if our well-read and clever authors of \u201cAnarchs Unbound\u201d would actually research the said time period, they would discover (to their undoubtedly great astonishment), that life in Russian village after the Reform of 1861 was indeed \u201cGetting Better\u201d (tm), with the spread of <i>Zemstvo</i> sponsored education and medical care.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong \u2013 there were a lot of enormous problems during Nicholas II reign, that finally resulted in the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolution_of_1905\" target=\"_blank\">Revolution of 1905-1907</a> (btw, why don\u2019t mention it and the Role Kindred played in it?). But what is listed in this paragraph by the authors \u2013 this is just plain wrong. Russia of t he said period could be a really scary place even without obligatory WoDish hamfisted grim darkness, with the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_famine_of_1891%E2%80%9392\" target=\"_blank\">famines in 1891-92</a>, the famine of 1901-03, the unsuccessful Russian-Japanese war of 1904-1905, Revolution of 1905-1907, terroristic actions by the &quot;<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SR_Combat_Organization\" target=\"_blank\">Combat Organization</a>&quot; of the party of Socialist-Revolutionaries (EsErs), that offed 2 ministers, 33 governors, 16 mayors; 7 admirals and generals and 26 police agents; the peasant uprisings, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potemkin_uprising\" target=\"_blank\">battleship \u201cPotemkin\u2019s\u201d uprising</a>, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moscow_Uprising_of_1905\" target=\"_blank\">the Moscow uprising of 1905-6</a>, the beginning of the Russian parliament, the vide variety of political parties that were present both as official and \u201cunderground\u201d Opposition. In short \u2013 a lot of excellent Anarch (and Vampire) material was just ignored. Why? What for?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The First World War greatly weakened the Tsar\u2019s hold over his subjects, and the power of the Tsarist Kindred alliance diminished with it</i>. </div> </div> </div>Okay, authors of \u201cAU\u201d, tell me this \u2013 how exactly the war that whips up patriotic fervor and gives a police even bigger authority to arrest, try and quickly dispose of the body afterwards (in the name of national security, of course!), the fact that the Czar personally took the responsibility as the commander in chief, the public shunning of all \u201cunpatriotic\u201d publications and speeches, somehow diminish the power not only of the Imperial Russian administration, but also of the \u201cKindred alliance\u201d? The only thing that perhaps weakened \u201cTsar\u2019s hold over his subjects\u201d was the <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prohibition_in_Russian_Empire_and_Soviet_Union\" target=\"_blank\">Dry Law</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>A sizeable coterie of Brujah ancillae enamored of the theories of Karl Marx had infiltrated Russian society just after the turn of the century, and as the Great War began, these insure</i><i>g</i><i>nts paved the way for later mortal revolutionaries such as Lenin, Trotsky, Kerinsky, Kropotkin and many others, first by helping to smuggle many of them back into the country after long exiles and then by covertly providing financial, logistical, and supernatural aid to their various revolutionary movements</i>. </div> </div> </div>Oh, there are so much wrong in just one (1) sentence, that it\u2019s simply unbelievable!<br /> <br /> First of all \u2013 what about the res of Russian political spectrum of the early XX centaury? Just don\u2019t tell me there wasn\u2019t any Brujah liberal-democratic \u201c<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadet\" target=\"_blank\">Cadets</a>\u201d, center-right \u201c<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Union_of_October_17\" target=\"_blank\">Octobrists</a>\u201d, chauvinistic anti-Semitic monarchists of the &quot;<a href=\"http://Union of the Russian People\" target=\"_blank\">Union of the Russian People</a>&quot;, <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Russian_Social_Democratic_Labour_Party\" target=\"_blank\">Social Democrats</a>, where both wings of it, both Bolsheviks and Mensheviks, claimed to represent the true Marxists teaching. Finally, wjat about the most known, badass, terroristic and popular among the peasantry party like <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Socialist-Revolutionary_Party\" target=\"_blank\">SRs</a>? It won\u2019t surprise me if the vast majority of Brujah (especially, the Russia-born ones) would support them from the get go. But Lenin\u2019s Bolsheviks? A marginal party that was in the March of 1917 pretty much obscure one?<br /> <br /> Next, how did a Brujah clan arranged something like<br /> <br /> 1) Safe passage in the closed car train for the Lenin, for his journey from the Switzerland to Petrograd through the Germany \u2013 with the German authorities agreement.<br /> 2) The passage forvTrotsky and 300+ of like minded \u201crevolutionaries\u201d from the USA to Russia?<br /> <br /> No, I\u2019m really interested how the clan that was incapable to act together from the nearly an Ancient times, would, <i>suddenly</i>, organize such costly and dangerous operation, that would require a level of international organization that is more characteristic for Termers, Nosferatu and Ventrue, but defiantly, not for \u201cBrujah-as-written\u201d! Or, how would Brujah provide any kind of successful help (be it financial, logistical or supernatural) to anyone during the Russian Revolutions of 1917 if they are so disorganized as a clan, with too many factions (even in one particular country) thinking that the \u201ccommon resources\u201d should be spent their way?<br /> <br /> <br /> And finally \u2013 did the personal beliefs and prejudices forbid our esteemed authors from checking the Internet (even Wikipedia!) from finding out that <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Alexander Ker<b><i><u>e</u></i></b>nsky was in Russia all his life prior the 1917 Revolutions and that he wasn\u2019t a Bolshevik \u2013 he was SR.</li> <li>Pyotr Kropotkin, besides that he was one of the founding fathers of Anarchism, was also a high-born noble who, also, didn\u2019t require \u201cBrujah\u2019s help\u201d in returning back to Russia (and if they DID arrange his return from the Switzerland, then see my complaints in the Lenin\u2019s example earlier)</li> </ol><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>The Brujah\u2019s plans for revolution were well-conceived and almost flawlessly executed, while the response of the Tsarist Kindred was weak, vacillating, and crippled by internal dissension. The revolutionaries spent years identifying the feeding restrictions of several of the most important Ventrue nobles, and when the revolt began in earnest, they were able to deprive these elders of their vitae sources. They were also able to locate the resting places of many Russian Tzimisce and steal away the soil upon which they depended for sleep</i>. </div> </div> </div><br /> Wait-wait-wait-wait here! What?! Did authors just in the uncertain terms said, that in 1917 in Russia there was only <b><i>one</i></b> Revolution, i.e. \u201cCzarists vs Bolsheviks\u201d? What about the February revolution, the one tha'vet toppled Nicholas II? Or, what, you decided that too much historically accurate information without crappy clich\u00e9s (\u201cBolsheviks toppled the Tsar!\u201d) would somehow result in the head\u2019s explosion of your readers, who have to face the horror of too much new historically correct information?<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see how these plucky revolutionaries managed all these amazing stuff. Say, how would they eliminate a heard of Petrograd\u2019s Ventrue who feeds on officers (good luck!), or, more importantly, who would they \u201csteal away the soil\u201d of Tzimisce. Especially the last one. If my players would come to me with such suggestion \u2013 I will undoubtedly allow them! Only to see how the \u201cHeartless Bitch Reality\u201d tears their plans in shreds \u2013 and them as well. But, I guess, here the Storyteller was either too generous, or such an attempt even wasn\u2019t played in real life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Within a few years, almost the entire ruling establishment of pre-revolutionary Russian Kindred had either met Final Death or else been forced to flee.</i> </div> </div> </div>Wow-wow-wow! Slow down here! So we have here something on par with the original Anarch Revolt, the total destruction of Camarilla/Elders power over 1/6 of the Earth, and, what, nothing? No reaction from the Camarilla? Not even \u201c<b><i>Blimey! Those dastardly Brujah Bolsheviks just have toppled the Camarilla established authorities from Warsaw to Vladivostok! We, as Camarilla, must do something decisive about the local Kindred, what not</i></b>?\u201d. Why this event wasn\u2019t called previously as the \u201cSecond Anarch Revolt\u201d? Why wasn\u2019t it called like that now, in that very book? Because the change that it describe is <i>monumental</i> (if true)! Just Google-search all of the main cities of Russian Empire. Then imagine that in 90% of them Camarilla\u2019s <i>ancien regime</i> suddenly (I have no other word) fallen and gave way for\u2026 something Brujah-Revolutionary. It\u2019s a huge territory with a lot of big towns, some of them quite ancient. And then \u2013 poof! \u2013 Camarilla just loost control over them. Is it so outrageous for me to expect some sort of reaction from Camarilla officials, hidden somewhere in the original WW cWoD books\u2026 or in this \u201cAU\u201d volume? \u2018Cause I can\u2019t find it!<br /> <br /> Imagine that! The greatest political catastrophe in the Camarilla's history since the 15<sup>th</sup> centaury \u2013 and not a word?! Either that or (or!) the change wasn\u2019t so widespread, the Brujah Council remained as nominal part of Camarilla and promised to respect it\u2019s Traditions and Protocols. But then where is confirmation of that? I can\u2019t find it in this new book! Or maybe (which is more likely) our esteemed authors just didn\u2019t give a damn about all this stuff and expect us all to accept their so-called \u201cwork\u201d as the \u201cnew well-though canon\u201d. Such plot-holey piece of donkey\u2019s dung? Thank you, but no!<br /> <br /> And our esteemed volume speaks nothing (nothing at all!) about the <b>SABBAT</b>\u2019s involvement in both pre- and post-Revolutionary Russia. I mean, how would they skip such a prize?! It was right here, during the Civil War the opportunities were enormous! But nooooooo! Authors preferred just ignore all that! Why?!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Soon, Russia was only one state within the larger USSR, an emerging global power under the dictatorship of Joseph Stalin, the first of several autocrats whose brutality served the Brujah Council\u2019s aims. The Brujah never directly controlled Stalin or his successors (or at least not to the very end). However, their devotion to Leninist-Marxist theory left them convinced that Soviet autocracy would eventually evolve on its own into a perfect socialist state, and they were loath to interfere in this \u201cnatural evolution,\u201d even as Stalin\u2019s policies led to the deaths of millions and Kruschev\u2019s brought the world to the brink of nuclear Armageddon. </i> </div> </div> </div>Where is the \u201cfacepalm\u201d icon here? Ok, this will do.<br /> <br /> You know, every author has his favorite subject. Like Mr. Achilli here. He wrote in \u201cClanbook Brujah Revised\u201d a lot of stuff, including, how, actually, Brujah had to share power with other clans, that Brujah Council (because in Soviet Russia it must be called a \u201cSoviet\u201d \u2013 a Council!) was a snake pit of political bickering. These facts were further corrected/retconned by other Clanbooks and supplements, that, finally, there were quite little from the original Achilli\u2019s write up of Russia. But here he got his chance to present his ultimate (and crappy as well) version of \u201cRussia by night\u201d! This time, he concentrated on Brujahs only. Sharing power with other clans? Oh no, what a ridiculous though! You can burn all the books that say otherwise! Hmm, and impressive pyre you got here\u2026<br /> <br /> And also, what about Kruschev who, supposedly \u201cbrought the world to the brink of nuclear Armageddon\u201d. For anyone even remotely familiar with the Cuban crisis it\u2019s quite obvious that the whole situation wasn\u2019t as clear cut as presented here, i.e. \u201cEbul Rushins are threatening the World! OMG!\u201d. And that\u2019s not even discussing the NATO\u2019s nukes in Turkey, deployed here in the spitting distance of the USSR (in the name of democracy, freedom and all ideals that the authors of \u201cAU\u201d express, of course!).<br /> <br /> <i>The Council never formally identified itself as an Anarch enterprise and both its brutal authoritarianism and its quiet bigotry against non-Brujah were certainly inconsistent with the mainstream Movement\u2019s ideals. But so far as the Camarilla was concerned, the Soviet Union and its satellite states were Anarch Free States in everything but name.</i><br /> <br /> And done nothing about it?! So, some upstart Anarchs from the \u201cGlorious USA\u2019s\u201d California demand a constant Justicar Prsence, but not entire Russia? A territory much (much!) bigger, populous and with longer history of Kindred settlement gets the official \u201cMeh, whatever\u2026\u201d?! I\u2019ve always knew that Camarilla Elders were senile \u2013 but this is a new low mark (either for Elders or authors)!<br /> <br /> <i>The defining characteristic of Soviet-style Kindred politics was a total rejection of the traditional, neo-feudalist \u201cPrince of the City\u201d model in favor of a national \u201crule by coterie\u201d government that had never been seen before and that was, as far as the Camarilla Princes were concerned, utterly terrifying. For its own part, the Brujah Council certainly considered itself ideologically allied with the Anarch Movement and would spend the next seven decades seeking to export Marxist revolution around the globe, as much to distract the Camarilla from attacking Mother Russia itself as to spread its own revolutionary dreams. For the Kindred, the Cold War that marred the 20th century was simply one more front in the War of Ages. </i><br /> <br /> Good! At long last we have another tidbit of useful information! That \u201cSoviet Russian Brujah\u201d ruled over their cities via \u201ccouncils\u201d, not the Prince (as if the term \u201cBrujah Council\u201d wasn\u2019t an enormous hint\u2026). That\u2019s nice! There is no more Princes in the Brujah\u2019s domains \u2013 but what about the rest of titles? Is there a Sheriff, or is his function delegated to \u201cTroikas\u201d? What about the Primogen \u2013 did the rest of clans still have a representative? What about the Keeper of the Elysium \u2013 did the Revolutionary minded Brujah even allow such title to exist? How did the \u201cCity Soviets\u201d resolved basic Kindred law dilemmas, i.e. domain disputes, rights of creating ghouls/progeny? There are so many questions \u2013 and no answers! ANSWER ME, BOOK!<br /> <br /> <i>For most of the USSR\u2019s existence, the Camarilla was not privy to the inner deliberations of the Brujah Council. However, Kremlinologists among the Camarilla know something happened to the Council during the 1980's. While the Council had permitted Leonid Brezhnev to rule for nearly twenty years, his successors, Andropov and Chernenko, were each quickly removed (possibly, some speculate, by direct Brujah intervention). </i><br /> <br /> Where is a facepalm icon when you need one? Oh, <a href=\"http://starbaseatlanta.com/ebaypics/stmangab20495.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">there it is</a>!<br /> <br /> What a pile of utter nonsense! Seriously? Vampires now are offing terminally ill soviet gerontocrats? What kind of crazy world it is!? <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andropov#Death_and_funeral\" target=\"_blank\">Andropov</a> was in \u201cworking condition\u201d for just 6 months! He spent the rest of his life dying! <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konstantin_Chernenko\" target=\"_blank\">Chernenko</a> was already dying when he became the head of the USSR. Killing them off for real would be a gesture of mercy on behalf of Brujah.<br /> <br /> Also, this passage (written, undoubtedly, by Justin \u201cI\u2019m a Vampire-God, baby!\u201d Acilli) totally ignores the information from other source books. Like, oh, \u201cClanbook Ventrue Revised\u201d (written, thankfully, not by Justin Achilli), for example, where there is said that caln Ventrue always maintained contact with it\u2019s members in the Soviet Union, even had a cordial ralations with them despite all this \u201cCold War\u201d nonsense. Beside the fact that this contradicts the assumption, that Camarilla totally abandoned Russia after the Revolution, this piece of information also points out that you don\u2019t need any bloody Kremlinologists (i.e., as demonstrated time and again, \u201csome charlatans\u201d) when you have \u201can insider\u2019s information\u201d via one of the Camarilla\u2019s well respected clans.<br /> <br /> But, nah! Lets ignore that!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>In 1985, Mikhail Gorbach</i><b><u>e</u></b><i>v took charge and immediately initiated a number of economic and democratic reforms.</i> </div> </div> </div>Not immediately, not initiated, not personally, not economic and defiantly not democratic reforms. Otherwise the sentence is perfect (in the West\u2019s \u201cGorby\u2019s Worship partyline\u201d at least). Oh, and this sentence full of love and adoration also misses Gorby\u2019s atrocious national politic, that resulted in Nagorno-Karabakh conflict. As a final note \u2013 I, as a Russian, personally desire to every Westerner Gorbach<b><i><u>o</u></i></b>v\u2019s lover\u2019s country to experience everything the USSR had experienced under his rule. With a personal Nagorno-Karabakh, of course.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Simultaneously, the Camarilla unexpectedly received word from the Council that it wished to discuss a possible \u201cnormalization\u201d of their relations. While the Council expressed no interest in formally rejoining the Camarilla, it was very interested in establishing some type of alliance against unspecified mutual threats. </i><br /> <i>Then, in 1990, all communication with the Brujah Council abruptly and completely stopped. Every effort to communicate with the Brujah leadership failed. Within weeks, any attempt to communicate with any Kindred anywhere in Russia was equally unsuccessful. By the end of the year, Clan Tremere reported to the Inner Council that all of its supernatural mechanisms for spying on the USSR had been rendered inoperative</i>. </div> </div> </div>[Sigh]<br /> <br /> So you\u2019ve decided to be \u201coh so faithful to the original\u201d and use Baba Yaga? How pathetic!<br /> <br /> Look, this all \u201cBrujah Council as presented\u201d is a weak written, crappy purple prose \u2013 nothing new here for me and for other\u2019s, who want to use Russia as a VtM setting. But reviving of Baba Yaga and of evverithing lame-o stuff indentified with her? Seriously?<br /> <br /> Lets talk honestly here, okay? All this \u201cBrujah Council of Russia\u201d was early \u201cWhite Wolf\u201d invention, because their game saw the light in 1991 when the USSR was still a country. And then it (suddenly!) collapsed. Our authors had very approximate knowledge about their own country, and atrociously low knowledge about Europe, and the non-existent knowledge about USSR and Russia. So, without straining their beautiful brains with some \u201cfacts\u201d (bah! who needs them, anyway?) they started to seek a plot device that would allow them both <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Describe Russia without tiring them with that dreadful \u201cresearch\u201d.</li> <li>Discourage players and Storytellers from further explore a territory that they, proud White Wolf, don\u2019t know a jack about \u2013 and have no desire to learn.</li> </ol><br /> <br /> Enter \u201cBaba Yaga\u201d and her \u201cPlot Deviced\u201d Shadow Curtain.<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause\u201d, thought WWs, \u201cthe Western Public is already thoroughly indoctrinated upon the \u00abIron Curtain\u00bb myth \u2013 it\u2019s stupid enough to accept as written this pulled from our collective posterior plot devise, that would make Russia (in the most ambiguous way, \u2018cause we suck at geography!) effectively unplayable.<br /> Oh, and we don\u2019t give a damn about them primitive Russkis in Russia that would have some troubles with running WoD games set in their countries. They are not human being\u2019s anyway!\u201d<br /> <br /> Either that or the inebriation upon a lot of restricted substances (my personal theory is that it was crack, that helped WWs with the metaplot for the most of the 90s, but I can\u2019t prove it) after which any shitty idea suddenly seams awesome.<br /> <br /> My personal opinion? Baba Yaga (as written) and \u201cShadow Curtain\u201d are just lame plot devices used in attempt to solve the obvious plot hole. It was true for the 90s, it is true now. The fact that WWs realized how lame their 2<sup>nd</sup> plot hole was (i.e. Baba Yaga as the big bad and the source of all evil in Russia), that they had to resort to the second plot device (and 3<sup>rd</sup> plot hole in the row!) just to get rid of it speaks volumes. So, I must ask \u2013 why revive something already crappy, plot-holey and lame?!<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t get me wrong \u2013 I think that <i>\u0411\u0430\u0431\u0430 \u042f\u0433\u0430</i> could be a terrific character for any WoD chronicle set in Russia \u2013 and not even VtM one. In Russian folklore Baba Yaga has so many roles, connotations and positions, that limiting her just tot \u201cDa Ebul Witch of Da Ebul Russia that has always been Ebul anyway\u201d is just wasting so much potential! If Joseph Campbell had known about Russian Myths and Legends while he wrote his \u201cA Hero with a Thousand Faces\u201d (a book that a lot of WW authors listed among theirs sources of inspiration) then Baba Yaga would\u2019ve find her rightful place in the \u201cAdventure Cycle\u201d. She would become a psychopomp, a First Guardian between the world of Humans and Others. She testes the bravery of all newcomers with her apparent command of magic, skulls with the gloving eyes upon her fence and straightforward claim of being a cannibal. But just with the right choice of words, some respect that is due to the elderly, with the performance of some quest or domestic chore she easily become Hero\u2019s ally and helper. Really, a more interesting concept, than what was presented by the original WW \u201cBaba Yaga\u2019s\u201d write up, do you agree?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>Simultaneously, and with a speed that stunned Western observers, the entire Soviet Union and the network of satellite states that surrounded it simply collapsed. Within the space of a few years they simply turned their backs on communism and adopted Western-style free market principles and nominally democratic political systems. </i> </div> </div> </div>Uhmm\u2026 How should we consider this? That Baba Yaga was totes pro-pemocratic/nationalistic/russophobic Revolutions that engulfed co-called \u201cEastern Block\u201d? Or that Brujahs, despite the evidence of supporting Gorbachov and allowing various dissidents to live, were the only ones who\u2019ve kept USSR/Warsaw Pact together? Also, what\u2019ve happened to the theory of \u201cVampires, really not influence real life politics\u201d that was adopted since the Revised?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>In the summer of 1991, the Camarilla sent in the first investigative team of archons to find out just what the hell had happened. Within hours of their arrival, all contact had ceased and no team member was ever heard from again. The same fate befell the second, third and fourth investigative teams, the last of which included a former Justicar. Since then, the Camarilla has given up on finding out what is happening in Russia and is reduced to hoping that whatever is responsible doesn\u2019t spread. Thus far, it has not, nor has it initiated any sort of hostile action or indeed any communications at all with the West. Tonight, the Camarilla ignores Russia and hopes for the best. </i> </div> </div> </div>Well, thank you very much, \u201cOnyx Path\u201d folks, plus all those authors you employ, that, perhaps in the past, had the experience with writing WoD books! Now it is official \u2013 thanks to your stereotypical vision about Russia, I can not stage any playable <i>and</i> canonically correct VtM chronicles set in Russia! Screw everything that Russian WoD fans (blissfully unaware of your \u201cdevelopments\u201d) have written about \u201cRussia by night\u201d, its history, current situation, clans powerbases and sects\u2019 plans. \u201cYe Olde Godes of Dev Team\u201d ruled that Russia is just another \u201cno-go territory\u201d, that they are either too lazy (or too ignorant) to describe in full. This putrid shit-piled \u201cShadow Curtain\u201d have worked 20 years ago \u2013 what should prevent it from working now, in our Globalised Age? No, what really, besides logic and facts, butwe have already ruled that out (as well as the opinion of Russia resident gamers)!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>While the destroyer of the Brujah Council does not appear to be a threat to the Camarilla, it has been devastating to the Anarchs. The Soviet Union had been quietly supporting Anarch-based revolutionary activities around the world for over 70 years. Throughout the 1990's, the Anarchs in South and Central America and in Africa suffered serious losses due to lack of financial and materiel support. Luckily, in the 21st century, help of a very different sort would arrive</i>. </div> </div> </div>No, really? \u201cSoviet Russian\u201d Brujah\u2019s sending \u201cmilitary consultants\u201d to Cuba or Nicaragua upon a ship? What kind of madness is that? And even if such operation was successful \u2013 where are the confirmation of that via older fluff of cWoD or something from that book?<br /> <br /> <b><u>Verdict</u></b>: This splat book just've killed any hope for a normal VtM game set in Russia. Just imagine that! You have a core book of VtM, no matter what edition \u2013 i.e. you have just enough information to portray clans and sects as they are, in their &quot;pure state&quot;, in the theoretical \u201cvacuum\u201d, without any local flavor or peculiarities. And then came the book, that, in theory, would widely expand your experience in playing one of the main Vampire factions that is so universally widespread.<br /> <br /> Instead you get a piece of \u201c<b><i>go-se</i></b>\u201d, that basically tells, that you were running your chronicles wrong all the time (with the additionall information how your country sucks as the cherry on the top), so you just are not interested in whatever else is written here. Net_Kindred? Oh, swell \u2013 remind me about them when they (and about 90% of other character groups presented in the book) would become available for my FUBAR\u2019ed by the official developers country.<br /> <br /> In short \u2013 \u201cAnarchs Unbound\u201d is bad. What is doubly bad is that it became a \u201cstrike from where you least expect\u201d. A Russophobic rant as the new official cannon for \u201cV20\u201d published in \u201cAnarchs\u201d supplement? Honestly, I didn\u2019t expect this.<br /> <br /> But still, there are still more atrocious \u201cWoD20\u201d books published by \u201cOnyx Path\u201d \u2013 and I will discuss them all in my next posts! Stay tuned!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3479,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","user":"von Lyttenburgh","date":". 07-17-2014, 02:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3479-von-lyttenburgh","name":"von Lyttenburgh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3479_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T00:43:59-07:00","id":199767,"title":"","content":"Fun fact:<br /> <br /> Your rant is ~5 times longer than the section you're ranting about.<br /> <br /> Anarchs Unbound isn't &quot;Russia by Night.&quot; It has a small blurb about the <i>failed</i> Anarch power grab in Russia. So it isn't even meant to be a play guide, but a snippet of Anarch history.<br /> <br /> Getting upset that a page and a half of text can't accurately portray an incredibly dense portion of history is a simple recipe for disappointment. There was, no matter how well researched, never a chance that Anarchs Unbound was going to cover that period of Russian history from both a mortal and vampire perspective in enough detail to ever make you happy.<br /> <br /> Gaming books aren't history books. Getting upset over historically inaccurate overgeneralizations, oversimplifications, and what not isn't going to get you anywhere, because the point of these books isn't to be a 100 level university text on the history of Russia. Hell, even a 160 page supplement just dedicated to Russia wouldn't be long enough to actually cover Russia from 1850-now in any semblance of accuracy. There's too much history there to accomplish it in a meaningful fashion.<br /> <br /> There's nothing &quot;Russophobic&quot; about it. Being inaccurate doesn't make it put down of the Russian people or culture.<br /> <br /> And... um, wanting to run a canonical VtM game set in Russia has obviously been a problem because Russia has always been &quot;off limits.&quot; The 20th Anniversary Editions aren't here to change major setting elements of the games. The Shadow Curtain and Baba Yaga weren't going anywhere. I'm not sure why you'd expect them to have.<br /> <br /> But who cares? Why do you need to run a canonical Russia game if that's not what you want?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-17T01:36:48-07:00","id":199802,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:red\">You were instructed by a moderator not to attack authors when critiquing books, and were suspended for one day:</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=196553#post196553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:red\">As a reminder, it is totally fine to share opinions, positive or negative, about WoD writing, but please make sure your critique is of the writing itself, not the person who wrote it.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">You returned from your suspension, and went right back to attacking authors:</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>von Lyttenburgh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/195709-wod-20-portrayal-of-the-real-world?p=199704#post199704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An author who is both prolific and lacking in writing talent, with, apparently, nobody to tell him about his drawbacks.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">I'm issuing a further suspension for personal attacks and ignoring moderator direction, and closing this thread. Do not start another thread on this topic.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}